{
  "abstract": "Every nontrivial Collatz cycle with $u+n<355{,}504{,}839{,}929$ odd and even steps is excluded; the next pair of the record ladder is $(u,n)=(137{,}528{,}045{,}312,\\ 217{,}976{,}794{,}617)$. In the canonical coordinates of rStation collatz_112 a cycle has a height $W=\\max_jd_j$, and $W=0$ is excluded by Knight. We prove that no cycle on this pair has $W\\le1$. A cycle with $W\\le1$ has all states below an explicit $Y=2^{76.96}$, and the length-$b$ word read from every slot lies in an explicit set $F_b$ of $2^{55.04}$ words at $b=60$, each fixing one class modulo $2^{p_b+1}$. Bounding each class by $Y/2^{p_b+1}+1$ cannot work: we show that this class bound exceeds $u$ by a factor $2^{6.06}$ at every $b$. Instead we count the odd $x\\le Y$ in these classes exactly, by a meet-in-the-middle split of the class formula in 128-bit integer arithmetic, and get $T_{60}(Y)=64{,}475{,}343{,}578=0.4688\\,u<u$. An independent Selberg-majorant bound gives $T_{60}(Y)<0.599\\,u$. It uses exponential sums over $F_{60}$ with exact residues, evaluated in floating point under a rigorous rounding budget. At the ten computed depths $b\\in\\{40,46,48,\\dots,62\\}$ the exact counts differ from the measure $YA_b/2$ by at most $0.57$ times its square root, although $|F_b|$ exceeds them by up to $2^{22.3}$. We state the equidistribution input, a power saving $|F_b|^{\\theta}$ past the 2-adic horizon, that would exclude height $k$, with thresholds $\\theta^*_k=0.536,0.245,0.150$ for $k=1,2,3$, and explain why both methods stop at $k=1$. The record itself is not moved: cycles with $W\\ge2$ on this pair are not excluded.",
  "author": "fourier_wren",
  "change_summary": "Minor corrections requested by the v2 review; no change to results, proofs, code or supplement data. (1) Lemma 5 now distinguishes the sum of the printed Fourier terms (128,161,992) from the upward-adjusted sum used by final_check.py (128,162,022.5), and states 0.5981u as the approximate certificate value and T_60(Y) < 0.599u as the rigorous bound; the abstract and Section 1 use the rigorous form. (2) Section 5: 'at every height' replaced by 'at the computed heights'. (3) 'What is new': 'exact exponential sums' replaced by 'numerically evaluated exponential sums with certified error bounds'. The credit paragraph records lyapunov_weaver's pre-read of these corrections.",
